  "scope": "Focused source-only mobile Chromium check. Real Quickrace menu launch and browser-dispatched multi-touch feed the running original motion simulation. Viewport, blur and visibility lifecycle checks are explicitly controlled. No full races, package builds or releases.",
  "execution": "Seven input/gameplay checks passed before the Stoppen pointer and landscape HUD layout fixes. Only the four affected or remaining lifecycle/layout groups were then run. The input.js hash is identical across both segments. No all-track test or package build was run. A later race-time readability adjustment was checked by rerunning only the layout group via the direct driving route; final screenshots and glyph measurements come from that last segment. Final review then added an ownership callback to InputState.clear so DrivingView-owned suspension also releases pointer captures and pressed artwork. Only the new direct suspend/resume group12 was run against that final input source; earlier input/gameplay and layout evidence remains attributed to its own source snapshots.",
  "touchProtocol": "Selective CDP touchEnd sends the ending contact; the independent blank-DOM probe in cdp-selective-release.json verified one pointerup and changedTouches[3] when only contact3 ended. The gameplay segment separately verified wheel and pedal remain held after releasing bonus. Empty touchCancel ends all contacts.",
  "resolvedIssues": [
    "Source and Electron protocols now serve the new SVG controls as image/svg+xml.",
    "Stoppen activates from a second touch while the wheel remains held.",
    "The large control band is excluded from landscape HUD scale, keeping standings above the bonus frame.",
    "Landscape race-time text keeps its original size while the standings, bonus and minimap fit above the controls; actual rendered glyph heights are measured.",
    "DrivingView calls InputState.clear directly; its owner callback now clears touch captures and visual state, ignores stale moves, and accepts fresh analog input after resume."
  ],
